<script setup>
import {ref,onMounted} from 'vue'
import {api,errorMessage} from './api'
const release=ref(null),error=ref(''),server=location.origin
onMounted(async()=>{try{release.value=(await api.get('/api/admin/agent-release')).data}catch(e){error.value=errorMessage(e)}})
</script>
<template><section class="card"><h2>Windows desktop agent</h2><p v-if="error" class="notice danger">{{error}}</p><p v-if="!release&&!error">Checking release…</p><template v-if="release?.available"><p>Version {{release.version}} · Windows x64 · Portable app</p><div class="inline-actions"><a v-if="release.files.exe" class="primary" :href="release.files.exe.url">Download EXE</a><a v-if="release.files.zip" :href="release.files.zip.url">Download ZIP with desktop shortcut setup</a></div><ol><li>Download the ZIP and extract it to a permanent folder on the employee PC.</li><li>Run <strong>Setup Desktop Shortcut.cmd</strong>, then open the desktop shortcut. Or double-click the EXE.</li><li>Enter server address <strong>{{server}}</strong> and the device name.</li><li>Read the capture notice and sign in with the employee account.</li></ol><p>The employee PC must be able to reach this server address. A local Herd .test address normally works only on this computer.</p><p>For updates, quit the agent from its tray menu before replacing the EXE. Keep the existing configuration and data folder.</p><p class="muted">This build is unsigned. Distribute it through your company's approved software process.</p><details><summary>Verify downloaded files</summary><p v-for="file in release.files" :key="file.name" style="overflow-wrap:anywhere"><strong>{{file.name}}</strong><br>{{(file.bytes/1048576).toFixed(1)}} MB<br>SHA-256: {{file.sha256}}</p></details></template><p v-else-if="release">No agent build is installed on this server. Run the release preparation script described in the installation guide.</p></section></template>
